        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758461,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Nintendo Wii, released in 2006, revolutionized the video game console landscape with its innovative motion-tracking controls and focus on accessibility. Developed by Nintendo, it aimed to broaden the gaming audience beyond traditional core gamers, prioritizing engaging gameplay over raw processing power. The Wii Remote, a wireless controller, became its defining feature, allowing for intuitive, gesture-based interaction. \n\nThe console boasted native internet connectivity and supported wireless connectivity with the Nintendo DS. Early models offered GameCube compatibility, though later versions like the Wii Mini streamlined the design. Blockbuster titles like *Wii Sports*, *The Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess*, and *Super Mario* series drove its immense popularity, leading to over 101 million units sold and establishing it as a social phenomenon. WiiWare further expanded the platform with digital distribution, supporting independent developers."
          },
